# Copy to `.env` and fill in. NEVER commit `.env` — this repo is public.
# The integrated product path uses ALL of these tools.

# --- Required for full stack ---

# Part A — Daytona H100 sandbox (ESM2 + clustering)
DAYTONA_API_KEY=

# Part B + dashboard Consult — Fireworks LLM (grounded observations + CopilotKit agent)
FIREWORKS_API_KEY=
# Optional model override (defaults differ by surface; see fireworks.md / dashboard README)
# FIREWORKS_MODEL=

# --- Strongly recommended ---

# Part B — Braintrust (optional remote); faithfulness always written to eval/
BRAINTRUST_API_KEY=

# --- Convoke MCP (optional) ---

# Convoke (https://www.convoke.bio) reached as an MCP server over Streamable
# HTTP. Exposed to the pathogen-pathfinder agent as the queryReferenceEvidence
# tool, for external background the loaded dataset cannot answer. Results reach
# the model as unverified public reference, never as laboratory measurement.
#
# Unset → the tool reports "not configured" and the agent answers from the
# loaded dataset alone. Get the endpoint from Convoke; there is no default and
# none is published.
CONVOKE_MCP_URL=
CONVOKE_MCP_TOKEN=
# Optional. Pin one tool by name; unset → the first tool the server lists.
# CONVOKE_MCP_TOOL=

# --- App surfaces ---

# Values above are read from THIS file (repo root `.env`) by
# pathogen-pathfinder/next.config.ts, which loads it at startup. A real
# environment variable overrides it; `pathogen-pathfinder/.env` is loaded
# afterwards by Next and is still available for per-app overrides.
#
# See pathogen-pathfinder/.env.example for that app's own keys
# (FIREWORKS_API_KEY, OPENROUTER_API_KEY, CopilotKit Intelligence).
